# Publish sketch / catalog (binding)

**Source of truth:** `README.md` § Add a new sketch; `catalog/README.md`; each `catalog/{series}/README.md` publish checklist; `docs/submission-and-series-structure.md` (show/year series).

Creating or shipping sketch HTML is **not done** until the full publish steps below are complete and committed.

## Layout (non-negotiable — enforced by `_scripts/check_catalog_mirror.py`)

```
catalog/{path}/README.md          ← catalog statement
sketches/{same-path}/              ← WIP + hub (mirrors catalog)
{path}/index.html                  ← optional short-URL redirect stub only
```

**Public series unit:** `{show}-{year}` (e.g. `marfa-2026`, `miami-2026`) → `https://mark-walhimer.com/{path}/`.

| Forbidden | Required |
|-----------|----------|
| Full project tree at **repo root** | Hub HTML at `sketches/{path}/index.html` |
| Root folder with real artwork (only redirect stub allowed) | Root stub listed in `STAGED_ROOT_STUB_ALLOW` in `_scripts/check_catalog_mirror.py` |
| SERIES HTML pointing outside `sketches/` | SERIES `../catalog/{path}/README.md` for catalog markdown |
| Inventing parallel folders “for GitHub visibility” | `github.com/.../tree/main/sketches/{path}/` **is** the GitHub folder |
| Skipping mirror because user said “own folder” | **Stop.** Explain mirror rule; do not move to repo root |

**Pre-commit + CI run `check_catalog_mirror.py`.** If it fails, do not commit or push.

## Hard stops

1. **Never commit or push** new/changed public sketch HTML without completing the publish checklist.
2. **Never treat** “file exists on disk” or “pushed to GitHub” as published — the catalog UI and `data/catalog.json` are the publish surface.
3. **Never move** a catalog project out of `sketches/{same-path}/` unless the user sends an explicit repo-layout exception with `check_repo_layout.py` update.
4. **Prefer** `_scripts/safe_publish.sh "message"` for publish commits (runs all guards + refresh + push).

## Publish checklist (required order)

When adding a **new show/year series** or changing work under `sketches/`:

1. `catalog/{series}/README.md` (+ `{artwork}.md` when applicable)
2. Hub + works under `sketches/{series}/`
3. Root `{series}/index.html` redirect stub (if shipping `mark-walhimer.com/{series}/`)
4. Add `{series}/index.html` to **`STAGED_ROOT_STUB_ALLOW`** in `_scripts/check_catalog_mirror.py`
5. Register paths in **`sketches/index.html`** → `const SERIES` (or **`sketches/catalog-work.html`** when that file is the SERIES source)
6. Available row same day — `.cursor/rules/launch-pages-available.mdc`
7. `python3 _scripts/reorder_series_by_index_mtime.py`
8. `python3 _scripts/refresh_catalog.py` → commit **`data/catalog.json`**
9. `python3 _scripts/check_catalog_mirror.py` (must exit 0)
10. `python3 _scripts/check_catalog_sync.py` (must exit 0)
11. `python3 _scripts/check_self_contained.py` (must exit 0 — see `self-contained-published-html.mdc`)

## Pre-ship checklist

- [ ] `sketches/{path}/` mirrors `catalog/{path}/`
- [ ] Root redirect stub only (if any) + allowlist entry
- [ ] SERIES lists every new sketch `.html` path under `sketches/` (not only the series hub `index.html`)
- [ ] Available row when the hub is a public launch
- [ ] `data/catalog.json` refreshed and staged in the same commit
- [ ] Mirror + sync + self-contained checks pass locally
- [ ] If user asked to publish: run `_scripts/safe_publish.sh` or equivalent full sequence before push

## Examples

- Marfa 2026 — https://mark-walhimer.com/marfa-2026/
- Miami 2026 — https://mark-walhimer.com/miami-2026/

New file `sketches/technical/foo.html` still requires SERIES → Technical, hub list when present, and `refresh_catalog.py`.
